# Push consumer nullable-group surface correction — 2026-10-14T22:38:45Z

- Removed the Rust-only nullable getter/setter aliases. The canonical Push
  config/facade group getter and setter now use `Option<String>` to preserve
  Java `String` nullability; updated Phase 10 crosswalk and compile-fail docs.
- Java oracle: `MixAll.object2Properties` omits null fields (`common/.../MixAll.java:348`),
  so Push running-info omits `consumerGroup` when the live group is null. Added a
  regression assertion against the local running-info body.
- First consumer compile exposed two running-info `BTreeMap` conversions and
  three tests expecting old getter/setter types; corrected those call sites.
  An initial null-group running-info test used the broker-routed API and failed
  with `InvalidRoute("null consumer group")`; moved the assertion to local body
  construction and restored a valid group before shutdown.
- PASS: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-consumer --all-features --locked`
  (219 unit, 9 admin, 2 facade API, 19 Lite/POP, 3 offsets, 1 orderly, 2 pull
  consumer, 7 pull-result, 1 push-pipeline, 2 rebalance, and 8 doctests).
- PASS: `cargo test --workspace --all-features --locked`;
  `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings`;
  `cargo fmt --all -- --check`; `git diff --check`.
- The full Phase 18 source/API/settings/overload/input/error/control-flow and
  reverse-export audit remains open; these gates validate the nullable-group
  correction only and do not close P18-V01 or any Phase 19 requirement.

